.TH RWP 1 "random word password"
.SH NAME
rwp \- random word password
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rwp
.RB [ \fIwordlist\fP | \- ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rwp
reads a wordlist and prints a passphrase of
.I COUNT
random words, joined by
.I SEPARATOR
and framed by
.I PREFIX
and
.I SUFFIX,
followed by a newline.
.PP
Only words whose length is between
.I MIN_LEN
and
.I MAX_LEN
characters are considered; when
.I ONLY_ALPHA
is set, words containing anything but alphabetic characters are rejected.
.I CASE_MODE
controls whether words are lowercased, uppercased, or kept as read.
.PP
Words are selected with a single pass of reservoir sampling, so memory use is
constant regardless of wordlist size and every valid word is equally likely to
appear.
.I /dev/urandom
is used as the source of randomness.
.PP
Without an argument, the wordlist named by
.I WORDLIST
in
.IR config.h
is used.  The argument
.B \-
reads words from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I wordlist
read words from this file instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-
read words from standard input.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The behaviour of
.B rwp
is configured at compile time by editing
.IR config.h :
.TP
.B WORDLIST
default wordlist path.
.TP
.B MIN_LEN ", " MAX_LEN
accepted word length range.
.TP
.B ONLY_ALPHA
1 to accept only alphabetic words, 0 to accept any word.
.TP
.B COUNT
number of words in the passphrase.
.TP
.B SEPARATOR
string printed between words.
.TP
.B CASE_MODE
CASE_KEEP, CASE_LOWER or CASE_UPPER.
.TP
.B PREFIX ", " SUFFIX
strings printed before the first and after the last word.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B rwp
exits 0 on success and 1 on error, including "not enough words in list".
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sws (1),
.BR swc (1)
